he rest of the input is background scattered with small shapes in several colours.\n\n**What changes inside the panel.** In each output, a legend row with colour c gains extra dots of colour c. The dots sit at panel columns 1, 3, 5, … (every other cell). The number of dots in the row equals the number of separate shapes of colour c outside the panel:\n\n- **Pair 1:** There are three colour-8 shapes, giving 3 dots. There is one 4 shape (1 dot) and there are two 2 squares (2 dots). The 8 shapes and the 4 shape only hold together through diagonal touches, so connectivity must include diagonals.\n- **Pair 2:** There are two 2 shapes (2 dots), two 8 X shapes (2 dots) and four 3 plus-signs (4 dots). The 4 shape is ignored because 4 is not in the legend.\n- **Pair 3:** There are two 1 triangles (2 dots) and one 4 shape (1 dot). The 2 square is ignored because 2 is not in the legend.\n\nThe legend dot itself is the first dot in its row (at column 1), so a count of n fills columns 1, 3, …, 2n−1.\n\n**Test input.** The panel is 9×11, and its legend reads 1, 2, 8, 3. Counting diagonal-connected shapes outside the panel gives:\n\n| Colour | Shapes | Dots in its row |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 2 (the two arches) | 2 |\n| 2 | 2 (the two diamonds) | 2 |\n| 8 | 4 (the four 2×2 squares) | 4 |\n| 3 | 5 (the five plus-signs) | 5, at columns 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 |\n\nFive dots for colour 3 still fit inside a width of 11.\n\n**Construction stages.**\n1. Crop the panel, which is the starting canvas.\n2. For each legend row, stamp that row's dot run, emitting one stage per row.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    # Stage 1: crop the colour-0 panel.\n    ys, xs = np.where(g == 0)\n    y0, x0, y1, x1 = ys.min(), xs.min(), ys.max(), xs.max()\n    panel = g[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1].copy()\n    emit(panel, \"Crop the colour-0 panel; its column-1 legend lists the colours to count.\")\n\n    # Hide the panel so only the outside shapes are counted.\n    outside = g.copy()\n    outside[y0:y1+1, x0:x1+1] = bg\n    H, W = panel.shape\n    for r in range(H):\n        c = int(panel[r, 1])\n        if c == 0:\n            continue\n        # Count diagonal-connected shapes of colour c outside the panel.\n        n = len(components(outside == c, diagonal=True))\n        # Stamp n dots at columns 1, 3, 5, ... in this legend row.\n        for k in range(n):\n            x = 1 + 2 * k\n            if x < W:\n                panel[r, x] = c\n        emit(panel, f\"Colour {c} appears as {n} separate shape(s) outside the panel, so row {r} gets {n} dot(s) at every other column.\")\n    return panel\n","candidate_tactics":{"objects":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The 8 shapes and the 4 shape only hold together through diagonal touches, so connectivity must include diagonals."}],"panels":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What changes inside the panel.** In each output, a legend row with colour c gains extra dots of colour c."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The dots sit at panel columns 1, 3, 5, … (every other cell)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The number of dots in the row equals the number of separate shapes of colour c outside the panel:"}],"legend":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Inside it, a single column (one cell in from the left edge) holds a vertical legend: one coloured dot on every other row."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**What changes inside the panel.** In each output, a legend row with colour c gains extra dots of colour c."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The legend dot itself is the first dot in its row (at column 1), so a count of n fills columns 1, 3, …, 2n−1."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"For each legend row, stamp that row's dot run, emitting one stage per row."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The number of dots in the row equals the number of separate shapes of colour c outside the panel:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The legend dot itself is the first dot in its row (at column 1), so a count of n fills columns 1, 3, …, 2n−1."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Counting diagonal-connected shapes outside the panel gives:"}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each output is exactly that 0-rectangle cropped out; the fact sheet confirms the output size equals the bounding box of colour 0."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Crop the panel, which is the starting canvas."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Crop the colour-0 panel; its column-1 legend lists the colours to count."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"9cee50483b7dd1bab6fb317e2469c8f882c42b90a72ff3af739b75cda5f61007","task_sha256":"e24de2db3d7791d736c216f272a0357d7ec3402aac5506fa99097d8b260f5411","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
